## Context

Filed from the replicator project on 2026-11-25 at the author's request:
"The skill should have templates as reference material. Intelligently
choose an appropriate one or IF NECESSARY propose another IN CONTEXT."
Child of tracker 1552.

Today `skills/replicate/SKILL.md` § report step 1 fetches only the General
template from Zenodo at run time and knows of no other. Zenodo holds three
I4R templates (search `"I4R Template"`, 2026-11-25), each as Word and LaTeX,
CC-BY 4.0:

| Record | Template | Version | Published |
|---|---|---|---|
| 23226406 | Reproduction Report – General | 1 | 2026-10-08 |
| 23214112 | Reproduction Report – Psychological Science Phase 2 | 1 | 2026-10-07 |
| 23597737 | Commentary from Forensic Report | 1 | 2026-10-23 |

Checksummed copies and an index are in replicator, `doc/i4r-templates/`
(replicator commit 217a541); the General one is the link on slide 5 of
Brodeur's pre-games deck.

## Request

1. **Templates as reference material.** Ship the three templates under
   `skills/replicate/references/templates/` with an index (record, version,
   date, checksum, CC-BY attribution), so the skill works offline and
   reproducibly, and the choice is made from known material.
2. **Choose intelligently.** At `report`, pick the template from the
   context the skill already has: the paper's field and journal, the kind
   of work (reproduction and robustness report vs forensic commentary), and
   any template named by I4R in the assignment. Record the choice and its
   reason in `manifest.json` (`template{name, record, version, reason}`).
3. **Propose another only if necessary, in context.** When none fits (e.g.
   a format or field none covers), say so and propose an adapted structure
   for this replication, starting from the closest template, inside the
   replication folder. Do not mint a new generic template in the skill.
4. Keep `references/rules.md` as the fallback where the chosen template is
   silent. Optionally check Zenodo for a newer version and report it,
   without switching silently.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The three templates and their index live under
      `skills/replicate/references/templates/`, checksums matching Zenodo.
- [ ] `SKILL.md` report step chooses among them from context and records
      `template{name, record, version, reason}` in `manifest.json`.
- [ ] The no-fit path proposes an adapted structure in the replication
      folder, with the reason, never a new generic template.
- [ ] `references/assessment.md`'s manifest example shows the `template`
      fields.
